<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line ltx_leqno">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">PaperRepro: Automated Computational Reproducibility Assessment for Social Science Papers</h1>
<span class="ltx_pubnotes ltx_pubnotes_meta"><span class="ltx_pubnotes_content"><span class="ltx_pubnote ltx_role_doi"><span class="ltx_note_name">DOI: </span><a href="https://doi.org/XXXXXXX.XXXXXXX">XXXXXXX.XXXXXXX</a></span><span class="ltx_pubnote ltx_role_conference"><span class="ltx_note_name">Conference: </span>Make sure to enter the correct
conference title from your rights confirmation email; June 03–05,
2018; Woodstock, NY</span><span class="ltx_pubnote ltx_role_isbn"><span class="ltx_note_name">ISBN: </span>978-1-4503-XXXX-X/2018/06</span><span class="ltx_pubnote ltx_role_ccs"><span class="ltx_note_name">CCS: </span>Computing methodologies Artificial intelligence</span><span class="ltx_pubnote ltx_role_ccs"><span class="ltx_note_name">CCS: </span>Computing methodologies Multi-agent systems</span></span></span>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Linhao Zhang
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
